<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Cayuga Nation</h1><p class="st-meta">1450 CE – present (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the five founding nations of the Iroquois Confederacy, whose homeland around Cayuga Lake in New York was lost after the American Revolution.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Cayuga lived in the Finger Lakes region of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, chiefly around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cayuga-lake">Cayuga Lake</a> between the lands of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/onondaga-nation">Onondaga</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/seneca-nation">Seneca</a>. According to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/iroquois-confederacy">Haudenosaunee</a> tradition they accepted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-law-of-peace">Great Law of Peace</a> in the mid-15th century, joining the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mohawk-nation">Mohawk</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/oneida-nation">Oneida</a>, Onondaga and Seneca in the Iroquois <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/confederate-states-of-america">Confederacy</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Cayuga sent ten chiefs to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-council-qing">Grand Council</a>, where they sat with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/oneida-nation">Oneida</a> as the younger brothers. Their villages of longhouses stood among orchards and fields of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maize">maize</a>, beans and squash, which by the 18th century were extensive enough to impress American soldiers. Clan mothers held the right to choose and depose chiefs. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beaver-wars">Beaver Wars</a> and later colonial conflicts Cayuga warriors fought alongside the other nations.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Most Cayuga supported <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolution">American Revolution</a>, and the Sullivan expedition burned their towns in 1779. After the war they ceded their lands to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> and scattered to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buffalo-creek-reservation">Buffalo Creek</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-river-ontario">Grand River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohio">Ohio</a>, from where some reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oklahoma">Oklahoma</a>. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cayuga-people">Cayuga Nation</a> survives in New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york-maine">York</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 1450 CE – present (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">North America and Oceania</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:88.56%;width:11.44%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1450 CE – present (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Fish Carrier</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Haudenosaunee traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Cayuga</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a>, <a href="/countries/canada">Canada</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Gayogohono, Cayuga</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1738&amp;focus=cayuga-nation" aria-label="Cayuga Nation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2269 765 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Cayuga Nation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="43